BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Artist in the Library Closing Celebration
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260926T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260926T160000
UID:6a75080e74e3b8b75db82b33@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The closing celebration will feature a storytelling dance and 
 drumming performance by\nIndigenous artists Nichole Leveck and Isaiah Cada
 \, and unveiling of the artwork created during\nthe 4 storytelling worksho
 ps. The exhibition will be on display for approximately 1 month or for\nth
 e duration discussed with the library branch. A simplified printmaking sta
 tion will be set up\nfor visitors to engage with the East End Collective a
 s they print graphics inspired by\nScarborough scenes. Guests are welcome 
 to get hands-on and take a print home. Jennifer\nLong will also be onsite\
 , inviting attendees to create artistic responses to the event alongside\n
 her
LOCATION:Taylor Memorial\, Meeting room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a75080e74e3b8b75db82b33
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
