BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Moonlit Magic 中秋节快乐:  A Mid-Autumn Storytime Adventure
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260925T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260925T113000
UID:6a4ffca74523092f002ed9bc@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate the beauty of the Mid-Autumn Festival with a magical
  storytime filled with enchanting tales\, Chinese traditions\, and the won
 der of the full moon. Children will discover the legendary Moon Goddess\, 
 learn about the festival's customs\, and enjoy stories about family\, frie
 ndship\, and togetherness. They'll also sing a fun Chinese song\, learn a 
 few simple Chinese words and phrases\, and create a festive craft inspired
  by the Mid-Autumn Festival. Join us for a joyful journey that brings Chin
 ese culture to life through stories\, imagination\, and fun!\nFor children
  ages 6-12.\nDrop- in only.\nPlease arrive early to secure a spot.
LOCATION:Locke
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a4ffca74523092f002ed9bc
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
