BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:3D: Design & Game Creation Camp (August 17-21)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260817T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260821T110000
UID:6a5fcd524523092f00319f01@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Calling all creators\, builders\, and future game developers!\
 nReady to take your ideas from the screen into the third dimension? Join u
 s for an action-packed\, 4-day summer workshop where you’ll learn to des
 ign 3D worlds and bring them to life.\nFrom creating your first 3D model t
 o dipping your toes into video game design\, this hands-on camp will take 
 your digital skills to the next level.\nWhat We’re Learning:\nDay      1
 : Tinkercad\n– Master the basics of 3D building and shape      manipulat
 ion.\nDay      2: Womp3D\n– Learn 3D sculpting to create smooth\, organi
 c\, and gooey      digital art.\nDay      3: Autodesk Fusion\n– Think li
 ke an engineer and dive into advanced\,      high-tech design.\nDay      4
 : Game Design Intro\n– Put your skills to the test and learn how to     
  create a fun video game.\nDay 5: Drawing with Dash\n– Use block coding 
 to create some simple shapes and do some free style drawing.\nThe Details
 :\nWho:\nCreative kids ages\n8 to 12\nWhen:\nMonday through Friday\,\n10:0
 0 AM – 11:00 AM\nWhere:\n[Agincourt Library/Learning Centre]\n⚠️\nIm
 portant Note:\nThis is a sequential\, cumulative program. Because each day
  builds directly on the last\,\nregistrants must attend all 5 sessions\nto
  participate.\nSpace is limited\, and spots fill up fast. Grab your spot s
 tarting on August 4th at 9 a.m.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe perso
 nal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library un
 der the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The inf
 ormation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery a
 nd evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information ca
 n be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\,
