BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Lego Camp
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260828T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260828T153000
UID:6a6cf574f213992f00c89117@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Special Guest Quantum Kidz Lego experts presents a 3 day Lego
  workshop\, building our past\, present and future. Each day will feature 
 a new topic. Come to one or come to all! Topics include:\nMonday August 24
 - Damsel's Knights & Squires: Take a step into the past as we learn abou
 t medieval castles were designed to keep the 'bad guys' out and the 'good 
 guys' safe and sound inside. Then join our Lego building master in buildin
 g with moats\, drawbridges\, crenelations.\nWednesday August 26- Under the
  Sea: Deep dive into a Lego adventure. We will learn about the poisoning 
 of our oceans with plastic.  Then build  anything you can imagine! Submari
 nes\, shipwrecks\, coral reefs\, sunken treasure\, Oh My!\nFriday August 2
 8- Where No One Has Gone Before: Join us for an our of this world day! We
  will learn the history and milestones of NASA\, including their planned t
 rip to Mars with humans aboard sometime around 2032…then build the futur
 e! Rocket ships\, aliens\, space stations\, rovers etc.\nAll supplies will
  be provided.\nIntended only for ages 6-12.\nTickets will be handed out on
  a first come first serve basis on the day of the program\, 30 minutes bef
 ore the program starts.\nDrop-in. Space is limited.
LOCATION:Maria A. Shchuka\, CPR
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a6cf574f213992f00c89117
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
